      "composition": "multiple-figures",
      "description": "Two engraved circular medallion rings joined side by side by a leaf clasp, each tied with a leaf knot at top and bottom. In the left ring a naked winged putto sits on clouds facing right with a flaming torch and a bow, a quiver beside him; in the right ring a robed winged child sits on clouds facing left, one arm outstretched, holding a tall cross on a staff. Acanthus tendrils spring from the four corners and two small serpent-like creatures curl under the rings. Black ink with hatched shading; the cream paper tone is kept inside the forms, the field inside and around the rings is transparent.",
